// Title: Publisher Attachment File Dropped In Suspicious Location
// Sigma ID: 3d2a2d59-929c-4b78-8c1a-145dfe9e07b1
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-08 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects creation of files with the ".pub" extension in suspicious or uncommon locations. This
//   could be a sign of attackers abusing Publisher documents
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of ".pub" files from those locations
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/EmericNasi/status/1623224526220804098
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_office_publisher_files_in_susp_locations.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Users\\Public\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Windows\\Temp\\" or FolderPath contains "C:\\Temp\\") and FolderPath endswith ".pub"
